---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ActionLink from "../../components/content/ActionLink.astro";
import ContactDetails from "../../components/content/ContactDetails.astro";
import ContentGrid from "../../components/structure/ContentGrid.astro";
import ContentSection from "../../components/structure/ContentSection.astro";
import PageHeading from "../../components/structure/PageHeading.astro";
import PageBody from "../../components/structure/PageBody.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/structure/SiteHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Visit the Seattle Museum | Connections Museum"
  description="Hours, directions, tours, access information, and group visits at Connections Museum Seattle."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <PageBody>
    <PageHeading level="h1">Plan your Seattle visit</PageHeading>
    <p><ActionLink href="/seattle.html">Back to the Seattle museum</ActionLink></p>

    <ContentSection
      id="visit-info"
      title="Visiting the museum"
      headingLevel="h2"
    >
      <ContentGrid columns={4}>
        <r-cell>
          <ContentSection id="hours" title="Hours" headingLevel="h3" headingScale="section">
            <p>
              The museum is open to the public every Sunday from 10 am to 3 pm,
              unless otherwise noted on this page.
            </p>
            <!-- TODO(issue): Confirm the youth donation amount and fix the awkward “$5 youths aged” wording. -->
            <p>The suggested donation is $10 for adults and $5 youths aged 12 to 18.</p>
            <p>
              While we are closed to the public for our volunteer work day, we're
              typically around to take item donations on Tuesdays from about 11am to
              3pm. Please email us in advance.
            </p>
          </ContentSection>
        </r-cell>
        <r-cell>
          <ContentSection id="tours" title="Tours" headingLevel="h3" headingScale="section">
            <p>
              Tours with volunteer docents start on demand, usually with little
              or no wait.
              Please note that our doors close at 2:30 pm to permit visitors
              enough time to conclude their tour. A quick tour can take one hour,
              but typical tours take up to two hours. For those with a keen
              technical interest, three hours or more in the museum is common.
            </p>
            <p>
              Returning visitors are welcome to explore the public areas of the
              museum at their own pace.
            </p>
          </ContentSection>
        </r-cell>
        <r-cell>
          <ContentSection id="directions" title="Directions" headingLevel="h3" headingScale="section">
            <p>
              We are located in the Georgetown neighborhood of Seattle,
              Washington, at
              <a href="maps:?q=$Connections Museum, 7000 E Marginal Way S, Seattle, WA 98108">
                7000 E Marginal Way S, Seattle, WA 98108
              </a>. It is an active central office in a large concrete building.
              Our entrance is around the side, a blue door under a yellow awning.
            </p>
            <p>
              Sadly, bike parking is limited at this time, but we are located
              conveniently on King County Metro Route 60 and 124, just a short
              walk from Stop ID #40871 and #46025.
            </p>
            <p>
              Our parking lot entrance is on Corson Avenue. Space is often
              limited, but can usually be found nearby at South Seattle Community
              College.
            </p>
          </ContentSection>
        </r-cell>
        <r-cell>
          <ContentSection id="other-information" title="Other Information" headingLevel="h3" headingScale="section">
            <PageHeading level="h4">Children</PageHeading>
            <p>
              We ask that parents with children under twelve visit the museum
              first, before bringing their children, to determine the suitability
              of museum exhibits for younger visitors.
            </p>
            <PageHeading level="h4">Pets</PageHeading>
            <p>We only allow trained service animals inside the museum.</p>
            <PageHeading level="h4">COVID</PageHeading>
            <p>Masks are welcomed, but not required.</p>
          </ContentSection>
        </r-cell>
      </ContentGrid>

      <ContentSection
        id="contact-before-visiting"
        title="Questions before your visit"
        headingLevel="h3"
      >
        <p>
          If you have any other questions before you stop by, please email us.
          For same-day inquiries, give us a call during our open hours.
        </p>
        <ContactDetails
          email="seattle@connections.museum"
          phone="+12067673012"
          phoneLabel="(206) 767–3012"
        />
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentGrid columns={2}>
        <r-cell>
          <ContentSection id="accessibility" title="Accessibility" headingLevel="h3" headingScale="section">
            <p>
              There is an accessible parking space in our lot. The museum
              entrance is at ground level, and a ramp and elevator provide
              access to the exhibit floors. Most public areas are wheelchair
              accessible, though some aisles inside the switches are narrow.
              Let a volunteer docent know what works for you. Restrooms are
              reachable by wheelchair but do not have grab bars.
            </p>
            <p>
              A tour can involve a fair amount of standing, and seating is
              limited. Tell your docent if you need a break; we're happy to
              adjust the pace. You can also contact us ahead of time about
              access needs.
            </p>
            <p>
              Volunteer docents describe exhibits aloud on every tour. If you'd
              like more detail, just ask. Some equipment is fragile or dangerous,
              so check with your docent before touching it.
            </p>
            <p>
              We can't provide American Sign Language interpreters right now.
              Many exhibits have text signs, and our
              <a href="https://wiki.connections.museum">wiki</a> has more on the
              equipment and its history.
            </p>
            <p>
              Please notify your docent if you need a quiet space during your stay.
              The second floor is usually quieter than the third floor.
            </p>
          </ContentSection>
        </r-cell>
        <r-cell>
          <ContentSection id="safety" title="Safety" headingLevel="h3" headingScale="section">
            <p>
              Live electricity is exposed in many non-obvious places, and rotating
              machinery can catch on clothing. Such is the nature of running
              equipment as old as ours-some is over 100 years old! We do our best to
              ensure a safe environment despite this, and all tours should begin
              with a quick safety briefing.
            </p>
            <p>
              Many of our artifacts are old and irreplaceable, but with just a few
              exceptions, we prefer to not put them away "under glass." So our
              simple rule is this:
              <b
                >Please ask one of our volunteer docents before you pick up items
                on display or interact with our machines.</b
              >
            </p>
            <!-- TODO(issue): Confirm a museum-wide policy for visitor filming and audio recording, then add it here. PR #13 raised this topic but did not include approved policy text. -->
          </ContentSection>
        </r-cell>
      </ContentGrid>

      <ContentSection
        id="groups-and-private-tours"
        title="Groups and special tours"
        headingLevel="h3"
      >
        <p>
          We'd like to make room for your school, club, workplace, or other
          group. If you're bringing more than six people, please email or call
          ahead so we can arrange enough volunteer docents. We can sometimes
          schedule visits outside public hours, depending on who's available.
          Tell us the date you have in mind and we'll talk through what works,
          including any suggested donation for a special tour.
        </p>
        <!-- TODO(issue): Confirm the per-guest donation for special tours before publishing Sarah's draft: "For such tours, we generally ask for a donation of $___ dollars per guest." -->
      </ContentSection>
    </ContentSection>
  </PageBody>
</BaseLayout>
